  "question": {
    "text": "A small block of mass <math> <mtext>m</mtext> </math> is released from rest from point <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math> inside a smooth hemisphere bowl of radius <math> <mtext>R</mtext> </math>, which is fixed on ground such that <math> <mrow> <mtext>OA</mtext></mrow> </math> is horizontal. The ratio <math> <mrow> <mtext>(x)</mtext></mrow> </math> of magnitude of centripetal force and normal reaction on the block at any point <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math> varies with <math><mi>θ</mi></math> as:<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/image13-05f109c8-035f-43b8-bd1c-910a6870.jpg\" style=\"width: 237px; height: 194px;\" />",
